  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 13,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.069,
            0.145,
            0.085
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "54"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.069,
            0.489,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.108,
            0.886,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "technique called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proof by Contradiction",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Namely, we assume the opposite of what we want to prove, and show that this assumption leads to a logical disaster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.171,
            0.611,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proof:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We shall explain the proof in steps."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.199,
            0.887,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 1: Assumption:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Assume "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a rational number. Therefore, it can be written as a fraction "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { p } { q } , q \\neq 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in its simplest form. (This means p and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are integers that share no common factors other than 1, that is, they are co-prime.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.488,
            0.305,
            0.568,
            0.346
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\sqrt { 2 } } = { \\frac { p } { q } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.351,
            0.605,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Square both sides of the equation:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.377,
            0.577,
            0.426
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "2   =   \\frac { p ^ { 2 } } { q _ { \\circ } ^ { 2 } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.426,
            0.509,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Multiply both sides by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q ^ { 2 } 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.451,
            0.573,
            0.474
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "2q^{2} \\equiv p^{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.477,
            0.421,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 4: Deduction",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p ;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.504,
            0.885,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Because "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is equal to 2 times some integer, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " must be an even number. If the square of a number is even, the number itself must be even. Therefore, p is an even integer. Let us say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\bar { p } \\bar { \\mathit { \\Gamma } } _ { \\bar { \\mathit { \\Gamma } } } ^ { \\mathit { \\Gamma } } 2 k"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (where k is an integer)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.578,
            0.804,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 5:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Substitute "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\bar { p } _ { \\parallel } = 2 k"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " back into our equation from Step 3:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.446,
            0.603,
            0.565,
            0.65
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{2\\bar{q}^{2}=(2k)^{2}}{2q^{2}=4k^{2}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.664,
            0.482,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Divide both sides by 2:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.463,
            0.687,
            0.55,
            0.709
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "q ^ { 2 } = 2 k ^ { 2 }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.722,
            0.886,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 7: Deduction",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q ;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Now we see that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is equal to 2 times some integer "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "k ^ { 2 } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " This means "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is even, and therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " must also be an even integer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.796,
            0.886,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 8: The Contradiction:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We deduced that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is even and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is even. This means they both share a common factor of 2. However, in Step 1, we stated that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { p } { q }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " was in simplest form, sharing no common factors!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
